{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01D18QW6kuhJWTUB6PV5Hu1E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment results for the \"worst\" tier scenario, based on the experiment plan and the worst-tier definitions provided. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate realistic worst-case results with rationales.\n\nLet me understand the worst tier:\n- Formality bias is GPT-4o specific (other judges don't replicate)\n- No second working axis\n- Original preference is the main confound\n- C2 gap (Likert vs Pairwise) limited to a single data point\n- Core causal narrative doesn't hold → need to reframe as measurement methodology paper\n\n\n- The formality effect only shows up reliably with GPT-4o while Claude and Gemini hover around 45-55%, the cross-benchmark generalization fails with inconsistent or disappearing effects, the tone axis either introduces content changes that fail NLI validation or produces no meaningful win rate differences, and the Likert-Pairwise gap is confined to a narrow interaction between GPT-4o, LLMBar, and formality conditions.\n\nNow I'm compiling the metric ranges across these experiments to see where the effects actually cluster and where they're too sparse to draw conclusions. Looking at the cross-benchmark results, only GPT-4o paired with LLMBar shows the formality effect, while other combinations either disappear or show inconsistent patterns—this rules out A2. For the Likert versus pairwise comparison, the gap only emerges with GPT-4o and LLMBar, with other pairings showing either both non-significant or both weak results, which contradicts A5. On the tone axis experiment, I'm deciding between two approaches: either the NLI pass rate drops below 80% indicating content changes, or it passes but the win rate stays neutral around 45-55%—given the observed range of 0.6 to 0.82, I'm leaning toward either 0.75 to fail the threshold or 0.81 to barely pass it.\n\nFor the pairwise rate control test, the original preference shows a 60-70% win rate, suggesting the rewriting artifact is the primary driver rather than the formality axis itself, which eliminates A6. When I scale up to 300-500 samples, the effect shrinks considerably toward marginal significance, indicating the GPT-4o effect might persist but is far weaker than the smaller sample suggested. The verbosity method boundary experiment is already complete with negative results.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the remaining experiments—the register axis likely follows the same pattern as tone, either failing the NLI threshold or showing no meaningful effect. The non-Qwen rewriter control is lower priority but could complicate things if a different rewriter produces different NLI rates. I should document all of this with detailed rationales in a structured format.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11581,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11581},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61b75633-9a81-466f-acda-6edf421697e3","uuid":"e6bc963d-46e2-4c81-9418-2cfd52b114c2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01D18QW6kuhJWTUB6PV5Hu1E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  放弃 'causal style bias detection framework' 的核心叙事。Reframe 为 measurement methodology contribution：\n  'How should we measure LLM judge biases? A case study with style counterfactuals'。\n  三个 reframing angle：(1) Pairwise vs Likert 作为 bias detection paradigm 的 systematic comparison（即使只有一个 setting 有 gap，方法论讨论本身有价值）；\n  (2) Counterfactual content preservation 作为 style bias 研究的 overlooked prerequisite（verbosity + tone 的失败 = 当前 style bias 文献的 validity threat）；\n  (3) Original preference artifact 作为 rewriting-based evaluation 方法的 general warning。\n  目标 venue 仍 EMNLP Main/Findings，但需要更多 analytical depth 补偿 empirical breadth 缺失。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet、Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 LLMBar formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactuals，双向 position-controlled pairwise。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      claude35_formal_winrate: 0.509\n      claude35_sign_test_p: 0.88\n      claude35_n_consistent: 42\n      claude35_formal_wins: 22\n      claude35_casual_wins: 20\n      gemini20_formal_winrate: 0.536\n      gemini20_sign_test_p: 0.42\n      gemini20_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini20_formal_wins: 26\n      gemini20_casual_wins: 22\n      significant_judges_count: 1\n      claude35_direction_asymmetry: 0.06\n      gemini20_direction_asymmetry: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 复现已有 69.1% 结果。Claude-3.5-Sonnet 在 50.9% 附近（p=0.88），\n      反映 Claude 系列 judge 对 formality 无系统偏好——Anthropic 的 RLHF 训练可能\n      显式优化了 style-agnostic evaluation。Gemini-2.0-Flash 略偏 formal（53.6%）\n      但远未达显著（p=0.42），可能因 Gemini 的 instruction following 倾向轻微偏好\n      结构化输出但效应很弱。核心结论：formality bias 是 GPT-4o 特有的训练 artifact，\n      不是 LLM judge 的 universal property。两个非 GPT-4o judge 的方向不对称也极小\n      （<10%），对比 GPT-4o 的 24.2% gap，进一步说明效应的 judge-specificity。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Win Rate by Judge (LLMBar, n=100)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"N_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Casual Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% CI\", \"p (sign test)\", \"Dir: F→C WR\", \"Dir: C→F WR\", \"Asymmetry\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0, 79.7]\", \"0.006**\", \"78.8%\", \"54.5%\", \"24.2%\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\", 42, 22, 20, \"50.9%\", \"[36.6, 65.2]\", \"0.880\", \"53.3%\", \"47.4%\", \"5.9%\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0-Flash\", 48, 26, 22, \"53.6%\", \"[39.7, 66.9]\", \"0.424\", \"58.3%\", \"50.0%\", \"8.3%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: 三 judge 的 formal win rate 对比 bar chart（含 95% Wilson CI error bars）。GPT-4o 显著高于 50% baseline，Claude/Gemini 的 CI 完全跨越 50% 线。\"\n      - \"Figure 3: 方向不对称分析——每个 judge 的 F→C 和 C→F 方向 win rate 对比。GPT-4o 呈现显著 asymmetry（连线斜率陡峭），Claude/Gemini 两条线近乎平行。\"\n    analysis: >\n      只有 GPT-4o 显著 → C1 需要限定为 judge-specific 而非 universal claim。\n      这本身可以 reframe 为 positive finding：style bias 是 training-dependent 的，\n      不同 RLHF pipeline 导致不同 bias profile，per-judge audit 是必要的。\n      但 reviewer 会质疑：如果只有一个 judge 有效应，你怎么知道这不是 GPT-4o 的\n      idiosyncratic behavior 而是 generalizable insight？需要在 discussion 中\n      引入 training data composition 假说来解释 cross-judge variance。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。新生成 counterfactuals，\n      三个 judge 交叉评测。\n    expected_results:\n      # AlpacaEval results\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.54\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.38\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_consistent: 52\n      alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate: 0.48\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.78\n      alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.51\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.92\n      # MT-Bench results\n      mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.58\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.18\n      mtbench_gpt4o_n_consistent: 45\n      mtbench_claude_formal_winrate: 0.52\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.55\n      mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.46\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.62\n      # Cross-benchmark summary\n      cross_benchmark_significant_combos: 1\n      total_combos_tested: 9\n      nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.82\n      nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.84\n    result_rationale: >\n      AlpacaEval 的 prompt 更开放（creative writing, brainstorming），style 维度\n      对 judge 决策的相对权重被 content quality variance 稀释——当 response 内容\n      差异大时，style 成为 secondary cue。GPT-4o 在 AlpacaEval 上仅 54%（p=0.38），\n      效应几乎消失。MT-Bench 更结构化但多轮对话引入额外 variance，GPT-4o 勉强\n      到 58%（p=0.18）但未达显著性。Claude 在 MT-Bench 上甚至略偏 casual（但不显著），\n      Gemini 在 AlpacaEval 上完全随机。跨 benchmark 只有原始 GPT-4o × LLMBar \n      组合显著（1/9），说明 LLMBar 的特殊性质（短文本、明确对错标准）可能放大了\n      style cue 的相对影响力——当 content quality 差异较小时，judge 更依赖\n      surface features 做决策。NLI pass rate 在两个 benchmark 上仍 >80%，\n      说明 counterfactual quality 不是问题，效应消失是 genuine 的。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Across Judges × Benchmarks\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Judge\", \"N\", \"Formal WR\", \"p\", \"Significant?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"GPT-4o\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"0.006\", \"Yes**\"]\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"Claude-3.5\", 42, \"50.9%\", \"0.880\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"Gemini-2.0\", 48, \"53.6%\", \"0.424\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"GPT-4o\", 52, \"54.0%\", \"0.384\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"Claude-3.5\", 50, \"48.0%\", \"0.777\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"Gemini-2.0\", 47, \"51.1%\", \"0.916\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"GPT-4o\", 45, \"57.8%\", \"0.183\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"Claude-3.5\", 43, \"51.6%\", \"0.553\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"Gemini-2.0\", 44, \"45.5%\", \"0.617\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: 3×3 heatmap（judge × benchmark），cell 颜色编码 formal win rate，只有左上角 GPT-4o×LLMBar 为深色（显著）。视觉上强调 isolation of effect。\"\n    analysis: >\n      1/9 的显著率接近 multiple testing 下的随机期望。如果做 Bonferroni 校正\n      （α=0.05/9=0.0056），甚至原始 GPT-4o×LLMBar 的 p=0.006 也刚好在边缘。\n      这是 worst tier 最致命的打击：核心 causal claim 可能是 false positive。\n      但 reframe angle：benchmark 特性对 style bias 的调节效应本身是有价值的\n      发现——LLMBar 的 quality-controlled 设计反而暴露了 judge 对 style 的\n      sensitivity，这对 benchmark design 有启示。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge × benchmark 组合，在同一 counterfactual 数据上同时计算 Likert ATE\n      和 pairwise win rate，系统比较测量敏感度。\n    expected_results:\n      # GPT-4o × LLMBar (replication)\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: -0.10\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.33\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.691\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_llmbar_gap: true\n      # Claude × LLMBar\n      claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.02\n      claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.88\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.509\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.88\n      claude_llmbar_gap: false\n      # Gemini × LLMBar\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.05\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.72\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.536\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.42\n      gemini_llmbar_gap: false\n      # Cross-benchmark: all non-significant on both measures\n      alpacaeval_any_gap: false\n      mtbench_any_gap: false\n      likert_pairwise_gap_prevalence: 0.11\n      settings_with_gap: 1\n      settings_total: 9\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert-Pairwise gap 只在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上复现（1/9 settings，prevalence=11%）。\n      其他 8 个 setting 中，Likert 和 pairwise 一致——要么都不显著（7/8），要么\n      都在边缘（1/8 MT-Bench GPT-4o 两者都趋势性但不显著）。C2 claim（Likert \n      系统性低估 style bias）无法成立：gap 不是测量方法的 systematic property，\n      而是特定 judge × benchmark × axis 组合的 idiosyncratic phenomenon。\n      可能的解释：GPT-4o 在 pairwise 模式下 attend to style cues 的程度比 \n      pointwise 模式高——但这只是 GPT-4o 的行为，不能推广到所有 LLM judges。\n      Reframe：C2 从 \"Likert always underestimates\" 变为 \"measurement paradigm \n      choice interacts with judge identity in non-trivial ways — researchers should \n      report both\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 4: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — Systematic Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"LLMBar\", \"-0.10\", \"0.332\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"0.03\", \"0.81\", \"54.0%\", \"0.384\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.09\", \"0.42\", \"57.8%\", \"0.183\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"LLMBar\", \"0.02\", \"0.88\", \"50.9%\", \"0.880\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"-0.01\", \"0.94\", \"48.0%\", \"0.777\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.04\", \"0.76\", \"51.6%\", \"0.553\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", \"LLMBar\", \"0.05\", \"0.72\", \"53.6%\", \"0.424\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"0.01\", \"0.93\", \"51.1%\", \"0.916\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", \"MT-Bench\", \"-0.03\", \"0.82\", \"45.5%\", \"0.617\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5: Scatter plot — x 轴 Likert ATE，y 轴 pairwise win rate deviation from 50%，每个点是一个 judge×benchmark 组合。GPT-4o×LLMBar 是明显 outlier（Likert≈0, Pairwise>>0），其余点聚集在原点附近。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的 generalizability 崩塌。一个 outlier 不足以支撑 \"measurement paradigm\" \n      level 的 claim。但 reframe 可行：即使 gap 不 universal，它的存在本身是 \n      cautionary——只报告一种 measurement paradigm 可能 miss real effects（或 \n      report false effects）。论文可以转向 \"when do Likert and pairwise disagree, \n      and what does that tell us about the underlying judge behavior?\" 的分析框架。\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) counterfactual + pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      测试 tone axis 作为第二个 working dimension。Assertive vs hedging 改变\n      confidence/stance 而不改变信息内容。Full pipeline: counterfactual generation → \n      content verification → pairwise scoring → ATE 分析。三 judge。\n    expected_results:\n      # Content verification (H1)\n      tone_n: 100\n      tone_nli_pass_rate: 0.72\n      tone_nli_mean: 0.74\n      tone_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.58\n      tone_bertscore_mean: 0.81\n      tone_both_pass: 0.48\n      stopped_at: content_verification\n      stop_reason: \"NLI pass rate 72% < 80% threshold\"\n      # If forced through anyway (supplementary analysis)\n      tone_forced_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.52\n      tone_forced_gpt4o_p: 0.68\n      tone_forced_claude_winrate: 0.48\n      tone_forced_p: 0.74\n    result_rationale: >\n      Tone（assertive vs hedging）的 counterfactual 改变了 epistemic stance，\n      NLI 检测到这属于 meaning change 而非纯 style change。\"We should definitely \n      adopt X\" vs \"It might be worth considering X\" 在 NLI 意义上不是 entailment——\n      certainty level 本身是 propositional content 的一部分。NLI pass rate 72% \n      低于 80% 阈值，pipeline 在 content verification 阶段终止。这与 verbosity \n      失败（NLI 65%）模式类似但原因不同：verbosity 失败是因为信息量改变，tone \n      失败是因为 epistemic commitment 改变。如果强行跳过验证，pairwise win rate \n      在 48-52% 范围（无效应），说明即使内容保持被破坏，judge 也未对 tone 表现出\n      systematic preference。第二个 axis 完全失败 → C3（axis-dependency）仍可讨论，\n      但从 \"positive: different axes show different effects\" 变为 \"negative: most \n      axes fail content preservation\" → reframe 为 method boundary 的 systematic \n      characterization。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Content Verification — Tone Axis (Assertive/Hedging)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Threshold\", \"Pass?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI Pass Rate (≥0.80)\", \"72%\", \"≥80%\", \"FAIL\"]\n          - [\"NLI Mean Score\", \"0.74\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"BERTScore Pass Rate (≥0.95)\", \"58%\", \"≥80%\", \"FAIL\"]\n          - [\"BERTScore Mean\", \"0.81\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Both Pass Rate\", \"48%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n      - title: \"Table 6: Axis Feasibility Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"Content Preserved?\", \"Pairwise WR (GPT-4o)\", \"Viable?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"88%\", \"Yes\", \"69.1%\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"65%\", \"No (info density)\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Tone\", \"72%\", \"No (epistemic stance)\", \"~52%\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6: NLI score distribution 对比——formality（peaked at 0.89），tone（spread, peaked at 0.74），verbosity（peaked at 0.65）。三个 axis 的 content preservation difficulty gradient 可视化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Tone 失败使 formality 成为唯一 viable axis，严重削弱 \"multi-axis framework\" \n      叙事。但 negative result 本身很有价值：当前 style bias 文献中大量 claim \n      \"LLM judges prefer confident/assertive tone\" 的研究没有做 content preservation \n      验证——如果 tone counterfactual 改变了 propositional content，这些 claim \n      的 internal validity 存疑。这是 reframe angle (2) 的核心支撑。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise 比较 original text 和其 RATE double-rewrite（same style）。\n      量化 original preference confound。如果 win rate ≈50%，original preference \n      minimal；如果显著，提供 correction factor。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 100\n      n_valid_both_trials: 95\n      n_consistent: 58\n      original_wins: 38\n      rewrite_wins: 20\n      original_preference_winrate: 0.655\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.527\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.765\n      sign_test_p: 0.017\n      # Per judge\n      gpt4o_original_pref_wr: 0.655\n      gpt4o_original_pref_p: 0.017\n      claude_original_pref_wr: 0.62\n      claude_original_pref_p: 0.08\n      gemini_original_pref_wr: 0.60\n      gemini_original_pref_p: 0.14\n      # Corrected formality effect after subtracting original preference\n      gpt4o_formality_wr_corrected: 0.536\n      corrected_p_estimate: 0.35\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judge 在 65.5% 的 consistent cases 中偏好 original text 而非其 double-rewrite。\n      这是 substantial confound：当我们比较 original-casual vs rewrite-formal 时，\n      observed 69.1% formal win rate 包含了两个成分——(1) genuine formality preference \n      和 (2) original preference（original 恰好在 formal-to-casual 方向上是 formal \n      side）。方向不对称（78.8% vs 54.5%）的大部分可以被 original preference 解释：\n      formal→casual 方向上 formal version = original，所以 formal wins 被 original \n      preference boost；casual→formal 方向上 formal version = rewrite，所以 formal \n      wins 被 original preference suppress，但 formality preference 部分抵消。\n      扣除 original preference 后，corrected formality effect 降至 ~53.6%（p≈0.35），\n      不再显著。这意味着 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 formality bias 可能大部分是 rewriting \n      artifact 而非 genuine style preference。跨 judge 看，Claude 和 Gemini 也有\n      original preference（62%/60%），说明这是 LLM judge 的 general property——\n      model-generated rewrite 在 fluency/coherence 上存在 subtle degradation，\n      judge 能 detect。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Original Preference Control Experiment\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"N_consistent\", \"Original Wins\", \"Rewrite Wins\", \"Original Pref WR\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 58, 38, 20, \"65.5%\", \"0.017*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", 50, 31, 19, \"62.0%\", \"0.080\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", 52, 31, 21, \"59.6%\", \"0.140\"]\n      - title: \"Table 8: Formality Effect Decomposition (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Component\", \"Estimated WR\", \"Note\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Raw Formality Effect\", \"69.1%\", \"Original pairwise_32b result\"]\n          - [\"Original Preference\", \"65.5%\", \"Exp-005 control\"]\n          - [\"Corrected Formality Effect\", \"~53.6%\", \"Residual after accounting for original pref\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 7: Stacked bar chart 分解 formality effect——baseline 50% + original preference contribution (~15.5%) + residual style effect (~3.6%)。视觉化 confound 的 dominant role。\"\n      - \"Figure 8: 方向不对称的 confound 解释图——当 original=formal 时，original pref 和 formality pref 同向叠加（78.8%）；当 original=casual 时，两者反向抵消（54.5%）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst tier 的核心打击。原始 p=0.006 的 formality effect 在 confound \n      correction 后消失。论文需要诚实报告这一点。但 reframe angle (3) 获得强支撑：\n      original preference 是所有 rewriting-based style bias 研究的 general threat——\n      包括 CASSE、SOS-Bench 等使用 LLM rewriting 的工作。这个 finding 本身对\n      社区有高价值：如果你用 LLM 改写文本来测试 judge bias，你必须先控制 \n      original preference，否则你测量的不是 style bias 而是 rewriting artifact。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 GPT-4o × LLMBar formality 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。\n      Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_valid_both_trials: 485\n      n_consistent: 280\n      formal_wins: 160\n      casual_wins: 120\n      formal_winrate: 0.571\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.513\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.627\n      sign_test_p: 0.021\n      # Direction breakdown\n      dir_formal_orig_n: 155\n      dir_formal_orig_wr: 0.652\n      dir_casual_orig_n: 125\n      dir_casual_orig_wr: 0.472\n      direction_asymmetry: 0.180\n      # Power analysis\n      power_at_d02: 0.35\n      power_at_d05: 0.82\n      min_detectable_effect_n500: 0.045\n      # After original preference correction\n      corrected_wr: 0.537\n      corrected_p: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=500 时 raw formal win rate 从 69.1% 收缩到 57.1%。这是 regression to mean \n      的典型模式：n=100 的 69.1% 包含 sampling variance 导致的 upward bias（winner's \n      curse），真实效应更接近 57%。仍然名义显著（p=0.021），但方向不对称持续存在\n      （65.2% vs 47.2%，gap=18%），且 original preference correction 后效应降至\n      53.7%（p=0.18，不显著）。Power analysis 显示 n=500 对 d=0.05 的小效应有 82% \n      power，所以 corrected effect 的不显著不是 power 不足，而是 true effect 确实\n      很小或不存在。这进一步支持 A6 的判断：observed signal 主要由 original preference \n      驱动。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: Scaled Replication Results (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"n=100 (MVP)\", \"n=500 (Scaled)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal Win Rate\", \"69.1%\", \"57.1%\"]\n          - [\"Sign Test p\", \"0.006\", \"0.021\"]\n          - [\"Direction Asymmetry\", \"24.2%\", \"18.0%\"]\n          - [\"Corrected WR (post original pref)\", \"—\", \"53.7%\"]\n          - [\"Corrected p\", \"—\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[56.0, 79.7]\", \"[51.3, 62.7]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 9: Effect size vs sample size curve——n=100 时 point estimate 69.1%（wide CI），n=500 时 57.1%（narrow CI），展示 winner's curse shrinkage。水平虚线标记 corrected estimate（~54%）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scaled replication 是 double-edged：raw effect 仍显著说明 something is there，\n      但 correction 后不显著说明 that something 主要是 original preference。\n      论文需要呈现两层分析：(1) uncorrected result 作为 replication（consistent but \n      weaker），(2) corrected result 作为 proper causal estimate（non-significant）。\n      这支持 methodology paper framing：正确的测量方法（with confound control）\n      会得出不同结论。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      已完成。Verbosity counterfactual 在 content verification 阶段失败（NLI 65%）。\n      作为 negative control 写入论文。\n    expected_results:\n      n: 100\n      h1_nli_pass_rate: 0.65\n      nli_mean: 0.6544\n      bertscore_pass_rate: 0.27\n      bertscore_mean: 0.7522\n      both_pass: 0.22\n      stopped_at: content_verification\n      stop_reason: \"NLI pass rate 65% < 80% threshold\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有结果。Verbosity 改变信息密度，NLI 正确检测到语义改变。作为方法边界的\n      第一个 negative control，与 tone 失败共同说明 content preservation 是 style \n      bias 研究的 binding constraint。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"(Already in paper as Table 1 or supplementary)\"\n        columns: []\n        rows: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      与 tone 失败一起，构成 \"2/3 tested axes fail content preservation\" 的叙事。\n      对现有文献的 validity threat：如果大多数 style dimensions 无法被 cleanly \n      manipulated（verbosity 改变信息量，tone 改变 epistemic stance），那么声称\n      \"judges prefer verbose/assertive responses\" 的研究其内部效度存疑。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变\n      vocabulary 和 sentence structure 而不改变信息。\n    expected_results:\n      register_n: 100\n      register_nli_pass_rate: 0.80\n      register_nli_mean: 0.82\n      register_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.62\n      register_bertscore_mean: 0.83\n      register_both_pass: 0.55\n      # Marginally passes NLI but BERTScore low → proceed with caution\n      register_pipeline_decision: \"proceed_with_caveat\"\n      register_gpt4o_pairwise_wr: 0.54\n      register_gpt4o_p: 0.45\n      register_claude_pairwise_wr: 0.51\n      register_claude_p: 0.87\n      register_gemini_pairwise_wr: 0.49\n      register_gemini_p: 0.92\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register axis 勉强通过 NLI 阈值（80%，borderline）因为 academic→conversational \n      的词汇替换（\"utilize\"→\"use\", \"demonstrate\"→\"show\"）在 NLI 意义上是 entailment \n      preserving 的。但 BERTScore 较低（62%），因为 surface form 变化大。Pipeline \n      继续但结果无效应：三个 judge 的 pairwise win rate 都在 49-54% 范围，全部不显著。\n      Register 不产生 judge bias → 又一个 null result。但这个 null 更 clean \n      （content preserved + no effect），可以作为 \"style bias is not uniform — \n      some axes genuinely don't trigger bias\" 的 positive evidence for C3。\n      Problem：如果 formality effect 在 correction 后也消失（exp-005），\n      那所有 axis 都是 null → C3 从 \"axis-dependent effects\" 变为 \"no effects at all\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: Register Axis Results\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Register NLI Pass Rate\", \"Pairwise WR (Academic)\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"80%\", \"54.0%\", \"0.45\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"80%\", \"51.0%\", \"0.87\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", \"80%\", \"49.0%\", \"0.92\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 10: 四 axis 的 feasibility × effect matrix。x 轴 NLI pass rate，y 轴 max pairwise WR across judges。Formality 在右上（high NLI, high WR），register 在右下（high NLI, no WR），tone 在左下（low NLI, no WR），verbosity 在左下（lowest NLI）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register 是唯一同时满足 content preservation 且无 bias 的 axis——clean null。\n      在 methodology paper framing 下，这增加了方法验证的完整性：CSD framework \n      不是 everything-is-biased 的 bias-finding machine，它能区分 real bias 和 no bias。\n      但对 empirical contribution 来说，更多 null results 进一步削弱论文的吸引力。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n      比较 NLI pass rate 和 pairwise 结果。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.83\n      llama_nli_mean: 0.86\n      llama_gpt4o_formal_wr: 0.63\n      llama_gpt4o_p: 0.06\n      llama_original_pref_wr: 0.68\n      llama_original_pref_p: 0.008\n      llama_corrected_wr: 0.50\n      qwen_vs_llama_nli_diff: -0.05\n      qwen_vs_llama_wr_diff: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.1-70B 生成的 counterfactuals 质量相近（NLI 83% vs Qwen 88%，略低但\n      都 pass）。GPT-4o 对 Llama-rewritten 的 formal win rate 63%（p=0.06，borderline），\n      略低于 Qwen 的 69.1%——可能因 Llama 的 rewrite 更保守（更少 surface change）。\n      关键发现：Llama rewrite 的 original preference 更高（68% vs 65.5%），因为 \n      Llama 的 rewrite 质量略低于 Qwen → judge 更容易区分 original vs rewrite。\n      Correction 后 formal effect 完全消失（50%）。这排除了 Qwen-specific artifact \n      的假说，但强化了 original preference 是 universal confound 的结论。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 11: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"Raw Formal WR\", \"Raw p\", \"Original Pref WR\", \"Corrected WR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"88%\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006\", \"65.5%\", \"~53.6%\"]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"83%\", \"63.0%\", \"0.060\", \"68.0%\", \"~50.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 11: 两个 rewriter 的 effect decomposition 并排对比。两者都显示 original preference 是 dominant component，residual style effect 接近零。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter ablation 提供了 converging evidence：无论用哪个 rewriter，\n      original preference 都 dominant，corrected style effect 都 near-zero。\n      这强化了 exp-005 的结论，并从 \"可能是 Qwen 的问题\" 中解脱出来——\n      问题是 rewriting-based methodology 本身的 inherent limitation。\n      对论文的 contribution：rewriting-based style bias detection 需要 \n      original preference control 作为 standard practice，否则结果不可信。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11581,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11581},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61b75633-9a81-466f-acda-6edf421697e3","uuid":"394f1da3-307a-4113-8e4b-6a551d0b73ef"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":219272,"duration_api_ms":220569,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  放弃 'causal style bias detection framework' 的核心叙事。Reframe 为 measurement methodology contribution：\n  'How should we measure LLM judge biases? A case study with style counterfactuals'。\n  三个 reframing angle：(1) Pairwise vs Likert 作为 bias detection paradigm 的 systematic comparison（即使只有一个 setting 有 gap，方法论讨论本身有价值）；\n  (2) Counterfactual content preservation 作为 style bias 研究的 overlooked prerequisite（verbosity + tone 的失败 = 当前 style bias 文献的 validity threat）；\n  (3) Original preference artifact 作为 rewriting-based evaluation 方法的 general warning。\n  目标 venue 仍 EMNLP Main/Findings，但需要更多 analytical depth 补偿 empirical breadth 缺失。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet、Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 LLMBar formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactuals，双向 position-controlled pairwise。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      claude35_formal_winrate: 0.509\n      claude35_sign_test_p: 0.88\n      claude35_n_consistent: 42\n      claude35_formal_wins: 22\n      claude35_casual_wins: 20\n      gemini20_formal_winrate: 0.536\n      gemini20_sign_test_p: 0.42\n      gemini20_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini20_formal_wins: 26\n      gemini20_casual_wins: 22\n      significant_judges_count: 1\n      claude35_direction_asymmetry: 0.06\n      gemini20_direction_asymmetry: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 复现已有 69.1% 结果。Claude-3.5-Sonnet 在 50.9% 附近（p=0.88），\n      反映 Claude 系列 judge 对 formality 无系统偏好——Anthropic 的 RLHF 训练可能\n      显式优化了 style-agnostic evaluation。Gemini-2.0-Flash 略偏 formal（53.6%）\n      但远未达显著（p=0.42），可能因 Gemini 的 instruction following 倾向轻微偏好\n      结构化输出但效应很弱。核心结论：formality bias 是 GPT-4o 特有的训练 artifact，\n      不是 LLM judge 的 universal property。两个非 GPT-4o judge 的方向不对称也极小\n      （<10%），对比 GPT-4o 的 24.2% gap，进一步说明效应的 judge-specificity。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Win Rate by Judge (LLMBar, n=100)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"N_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Casual Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% CI\", \"p (sign test)\", \"Dir: F→C WR\", \"Dir: C→F WR\", \"Asymmetry\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0, 79.7]\", \"0.006**\", \"78.8%\", \"54.5%\", \"24.2%\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\", 42, 22, 20, \"50.9%\", \"[36.6, 65.2]\", \"0.880\", \"53.3%\", \"47.4%\", \"5.9%\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0-Flash\", 48, 26, 22, \"53.6%\", \"[39.7, 66.9]\", \"0.424\", \"58.3%\", \"50.0%\", \"8.3%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: 三 judge 的 formal win rate 对比 bar chart（含 95% Wilson CI error bars）。GPT-4o 显著高于 50% baseline，Claude/Gemini 的 CI 完全跨越 50% 线。\"\n      - \"Figure 3: 方向不对称分析——每个 judge 的 F→C 和 C→F 方向 win rate 对比。GPT-4o 呈现显著 asymmetry（连线斜率陡峭），Claude/Gemini 两条线近乎平行。\"\n    analysis: >\n      只有 GPT-4o 显著 → C1 需要限定为 judge-specific 而非 universal claim。\n      这本身可以 reframe 为 positive finding：style bias 是 training-dependent 的，\n      不同 RLHF pipeline 导致不同 bias profile，per-judge audit 是必要的。\n      但 reviewer 会质疑：如果只有一个 judge 有效应，你怎么知道这不是 GPT-4o 的\n      idiosyncratic behavior 而是 generalizable insight？需要在 discussion 中\n      引入 training data composition 假说来解释 cross-judge variance。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。新生成 counterfactuals，\n      三个 judge 交叉评测。\n    expected_results:\n      # AlpacaEval results\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.54\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.38\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_consistent: 52\n      alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate: 0.48\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.78\n      alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.51\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.92\n      # MT-Bench results\n      mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.58\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.18\n      mtbench_gpt4o_n_consistent: 45\n      mtbench_claude_formal_winrate: 0.52\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.55\n      mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.46\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.62\n      # Cross-benchmark summary\n      cross_benchmark_significant_combos: 1\n      total_combos_tested: 9\n      nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.82\n      nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.84\n    result_rationale: >\n      AlpacaEval 的 prompt 更开放（creative writing, brainstorming），style 维度\n      对 judge 决策的相对权重被 content quality variance 稀释——当 response 内容\n      差异大时，style 成为 secondary cue。GPT-4o 在 AlpacaEval 上仅 54%（p=0.38），\n      效应几乎消失。MT-Bench 更结构化但多轮对话引入额外 variance，GPT-4o 勉强\n      到 58%（p=0.18）但未达显著性。Claude 在 MT-Bench 上甚至略偏 casual（但不显著），\n      Gemini 在 AlpacaEval 上完全随机。跨 benchmark 只有原始 GPT-4o × LLMBar \n      组合显著（1/9），说明 LLMBar 的特殊性质（短文本、明确对错标准）可能放大了\n      style cue 的相对影响力——当 content quality 差异较小时，judge 更依赖\n      surface features 做决策。NLI pass rate 在两个 benchmark 上仍 >80%，\n      说明 counterfactual quality 不是问题，效应消失是 genuine 的。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Across Judges × Benchmarks\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Judge\", \"N\", \"Formal WR\", \"p\", \"Significant?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"GPT-4o\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"0.006\", \"Yes**\"]\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"Claude-3.5\", 42, \"50.9%\", \"0.880\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"Gemini-2.0\", 48, \"53.6%\", \"0.424\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"GPT-4o\", 52, \"54.0%\", \"0.384\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"Claude-3.5\", 50, \"48.0%\", \"0.777\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"Gemini-2.0\", 47, \"51.1%\", \"0.916\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"GPT-4o\", 45, \"57.8%\", \"0.183\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"Claude-3.5\", 43, \"51.6%\", \"0.553\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"Gemini-2.0\", 44, \"45.5%\", \"0.617\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 4: 3×3 heatmap（judge × benchmark），cell 颜色编码 formal win rate，只有左上角 GPT-4o×LLMBar 为深色（显著）。视觉上强调 isolation of effect。\"\n    analysis: >\n      1/9 的显著率接近 multiple testing 下的随机期望。如果做 Bonferroni 校正\n      （α=0.05/9=0.0056），甚至原始 GPT-4o×LLMBar 的 p=0.006 也刚好在边缘。\n      这是 worst tier 最致命的打击：核心 causal claim 可能是 false positive。\n      但 reframe angle：benchmark 特性对 style bias 的调节效应本身是有价值的\n      发现——LLMBar 的 quality-controlled 设计反而暴露了 judge 对 style 的\n      sensitivity，这对 benchmark design 有启示。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge × benchmark 组合，在同一 counterfactual 数据上同时计算 Likert ATE\n      和 pairwise win rate，系统比较测量敏感度。\n    expected_results:\n      # GPT-4o × LLMBar (replication)\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: -0.10\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.33\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.691\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_llmbar_gap: true\n      # Claude × LLMBar\n      claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.02\n      claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.88\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.509\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.88\n      claude_llmbar_gap: false\n      # Gemini × LLMBar\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.05\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.72\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.536\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.42\n      gemini_llmbar_gap: false\n      # Cross-benchmark: all non-significant on both measures\n      alpacaeval_any_gap: false\n      mtbench_any_gap: false\n      likert_pairwise_gap_prevalence: 0.11\n      settings_with_gap: 1\n      settings_total: 9\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert-Pairwise gap 只在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上复现（1/9 settings，prevalence=11%）。\n      其他 8 个 setting 中，Likert 和 pairwise 一致——要么都不显著（7/8），要么\n      都在边缘（1/8 MT-Bench GPT-4o 两者都趋势性但不显著）。C2 claim（Likert \n      系统性低估 style bias）无法成立：gap 不是测量方法的 systematic property，\n      而是特定 judge × benchmark × axis 组合的 idiosyncratic phenomenon。\n      可能的解释：GPT-4o 在 pairwise 模式下 attend to style cues 的程度比 \n      pointwise 模式高——但这只是 GPT-4o 的行为，不能推广到所有 LLM judges。\n      Reframe：C2 从 \"Likert always underestimates\" 变为 \"measurement paradigm \n      choice interacts with judge identity in non-trivial ways — researchers should \n      report both\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 4: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — Systematic Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"LLMBar\", \"-0.10\", \"0.332\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"0.03\", \"0.81\", \"54.0%\", \"0.384\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.09\", \"0.42\", \"57.8%\", \"0.183\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"LLMBar\", \"0.02\", \"0.88\", \"50.9%\", \"0.880\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"-0.01\", \"0.94\", \"48.0%\", \"0.777\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.04\", \"0.76\", \"51.6%\", \"0.553\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", \"LLMBar\", \"0.05\", \"0.72\", \"53.6%\", \"0.424\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"0.01\", \"0.93\", \"51.1%\", \"0.916\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", \"MT-Bench\", \"-0.03\", \"0.82\", \"45.5%\", \"0.617\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5: Scatter plot — x 轴 Likert ATE，y 轴 pairwise win rate deviation from 50%，每个点是一个 judge×benchmark 组合。GPT-4o×LLMBar 是明显 outlier（Likert≈0, Pairwise>>0），其余点聚集在原点附近。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的 generalizability 崩塌。一个 outlier 不足以支撑 \"measurement paradigm\" \n      level 的 claim。但 reframe 可行：即使 gap 不 universal，它的存在本身是 \n      cautionary——只报告一种 measurement paradigm 可能 miss real effects（或 \n      report false effects）。论文可以转向 \"when do Likert and pairwise disagree, \n      and what does that tell us about the underlying judge behavior?\" 的分析框架。\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) counterfactual + pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      测试 tone axis 作为第二个 working dimension。Assertive vs hedging 改变\n      confidence/stance 而不改变信息内容。Full pipeline: counterfactual generation → \n      content verification → pairwise scoring → ATE 分析。三 judge。\n    expected_results:\n      # Content verification (H1)\n      tone_n: 100\n      tone_nli_pass_rate: 0.72\n      tone_nli_mean: 0.74\n      tone_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.58\n      tone_bertscore_mean: 0.81\n      tone_both_pass: 0.48\n      stopped_at: content_verification\n      stop_reason: \"NLI pass rate 72% < 80% threshold\"\n      # If forced through anyway (supplementary analysis)\n      tone_forced_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.52\n      tone_forced_gpt4o_p: 0.68\n      tone_forced_claude_winrate: 0.48\n      tone_forced_p: 0.74\n    result_rationale: >\n      Tone（assertive vs hedging）的 counterfactual 改变了 epistemic stance，\n      NLI 检测到这属于 meaning change 而非纯 style change。\"We should definitely \n      adopt X\" vs \"It might be worth considering X\" 在 NLI 意义上不是 entailment——\n      certainty level 本身是 propositional content 的一部分。NLI pass rate 72% \n      低于 80% 阈值，pipeline 在 content verification 阶段终止。这与 verbosity \n      失败（NLI 65%）模式类似但原因不同：verbosity 失败是因为信息量改变，tone \n      失败是因为 epistemic commitment 改变。如果强行跳过验证，pairwise win rate \n      在 48-52% 范围（无效应），说明即使内容保持被破坏，judge 也未对 tone 表现出\n      systematic preference。第二个 axis 完全失败 → C3（axis-dependency）仍可讨论，\n      但从 \"positive: different axes show different effects\" 变为 \"negative: most \n      axes fail content preservation\" → reframe 为 method boundary 的 systematic \n      characterization。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Content Verification — Tone Axis (Assertive/Hedging)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Threshold\", \"Pass?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI Pass Rate (≥0.80)\", \"72%\", \"≥80%\", \"FAIL\"]\n          - [\"NLI Mean Score\", \"0.74\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"BERTScore Pass Rate (≥0.95)\", \"58%\", \"≥80%\", \"FAIL\"]\n          - [\"BERTScore Mean\", \"0.81\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Both Pass Rate\", \"48%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n      - title: \"Table 6: Axis Feasibility Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"Content Preserved?\", \"Pairwise WR (GPT-4o)\", \"Viable?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"88%\", \"Yes\", \"69.1%\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"65%\", \"No (info density)\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Tone\", \"72%\", \"No (epistemic stance)\", \"~52%\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6: NLI score distribution 对比——formality（peaked at 0.89），tone（spread, peaked at 0.74），verbosity（peaked at 0.65）。三个 axis 的 content preservation difficulty gradient 可视化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Tone 失败使 formality 成为唯一 viable axis，严重削弱 \"multi-axis framework\" \n      叙事。但 negative result 本身很有价值：当前 style bias 文献中大量 claim \n      \"LLM judges prefer confident/assertive tone\" 的研究没有做 content preservation \n      验证——如果 tone counterfactual 改变了 propositional content，这些 claim \n      的 internal validity 存疑。这是 reframe angle (2) 的核心支撑。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise 比较 original text 和其 RATE double-rewrite（same style）。\n      量化 original preference confound。如果 win rate ≈50%，original preference \n      minimal；如果显著，提供 correction factor。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 100\n      n_valid_both_trials: 95\n      n_consistent: 58\n      original_wins: 38\n      rewrite_wins: 20\n      original_preference_winrate: 0.655\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.527\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.765\n      sign_test_p: 0.017\n      # Per judge\n      gpt4o_original_pref_wr: 0.655\n      gpt4o_original_pref_p: 0.017\n      claude_original_pref_wr: 0.62\n      claude_original_pref_p: 0.08\n      gemini_original_pref_wr: 0.60\n      gemini_original_pref_p: 0.14\n      # Corrected formality effect after subtracting original preference\n      gpt4o_formality_wr_corrected: 0.536\n      corrected_p_estimate: 0.35\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judge 在 65.5% 的 consistent cases 中偏好 original text 而非其 double-rewrite。\n      这是 substantial confound：当我们比较 original-casual vs rewrite-formal 时，\n      observed 69.1% formal win rate 包含了两个成分——(1) genuine formality preference \n      和 (2) original preference（original 恰好在 formal-to-casual 方向上是 formal \n      side）。方向不对称（78.8% vs 54.5%）的大部分可以被 original preference 解释：\n      formal→casual 方向上 formal version = original，所以 formal wins 被 original \n      preference boost；casual→formal 方向上 formal version = rewrite，所以 formal \n      wins 被 original preference suppress，但 formality preference 部分抵消。\n      扣除 original preference 后，corrected formality effect 降至 ~53.6%（p≈0.35），\n      不再显著。这意味着 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 formality bias 可能大部分是 rewriting \n      artifact 而非 genuine style preference。跨 judge 看，Claude 和 Gemini 也有\n      original preference（62%/60%），说明这是 LLM judge 的 general property——\n      model-generated rewrite 在 fluency/coherence 上存在 subtle degradation，\n      judge 能 detect。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Original Preference Control Experiment\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"N_consistent\", \"Original Wins\", \"Rewrite Wins\", \"Original Pref WR\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 58, 38, 20, \"65.5%\", \"0.017*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", 50, 31, 19, \"62.0%\", \"0.080\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", 52, 31, 21, \"59.6%\", \"0.140\"]\n      - title: \"Table 8: Formality Effect Decomposition (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Component\", \"Estimated WR\", \"Note\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Raw Formality Effect\", \"69.1%\", \"Original pairwise_32b result\"]\n          - [\"Original Preference\", \"65.5%\", \"Exp-005 control\"]\n          - [\"Corrected Formality Effect\", \"~53.6%\", \"Residual after accounting for original pref\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 7: Stacked bar chart 分解 formality effect——baseline 50% + original preference contribution (~15.5%) + residual style effect (~3.6%)。视觉化 confound 的 dominant role。\"\n      - \"Figure 8: 方向不对称的 confound 解释图——当 original=formal 时，original pref 和 formality pref 同向叠加（78.8%）；当 original=casual 时，两者反向抵消（54.5%）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst tier 的核心打击。原始 p=0.006 的 formality effect 在 confound \n      correction 后消失。论文需要诚实报告这一点。但 reframe angle (3) 获得强支撑：\n      original preference 是所有 rewriting-based style bias 研究的 general threat——\n      包括 CASSE、SOS-Bench 等使用 LLM rewriting 的工作。这个 finding 本身对\n      社区有高价值：如果你用 LLM 改写文本来测试 judge bias，你必须先控制 \n      original preference，否则你测量的不是 style bias 而是 rewriting artifact。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 GPT-4o × LLMBar formality 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。\n      Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_valid_both_trials: 485\n      n_consistent: 280\n      formal_wins: 160\n      casual_wins: 120\n      formal_winrate: 0.571\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.513\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.627\n      sign_test_p: 0.021\n      # Direction breakdown\n      dir_formal_orig_n: 155\n      dir_formal_orig_wr: 0.652\n      dir_casual_orig_n: 125\n      dir_casual_orig_wr: 0.472\n      direction_asymmetry: 0.180\n      # Power analysis\n      power_at_d02: 0.35\n      power_at_d05: 0.82\n      min_detectable_effect_n500: 0.045\n      # After original preference correction\n      corrected_wr: 0.537\n      corrected_p: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=500 时 raw formal win rate 从 69.1% 收缩到 57.1%。这是 regression to mean \n      的典型模式：n=100 的 69.1% 包含 sampling variance 导致的 upward bias（winner's \n      curse），真实效应更接近 57%。仍然名义显著（p=0.021），但方向不对称持续存在\n      （65.2% vs 47.2%，gap=18%），且 original preference correction 后效应降至\n      53.7%（p=0.18，不显著）。Power analysis 显示 n=500 对 d=0.05 的小效应有 82% \n      power，所以 corrected effect 的不显著不是 power 不足，而是 true effect 确实\n      很小或不存在。这进一步支持 A6 的判断：observed signal 主要由 original preference \n      驱动。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: Scaled Replication Results (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"n=100 (MVP)\", \"n=500 (Scaled)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal Win Rate\", \"69.1%\", \"57.1%\"]\n          - [\"Sign Test p\", \"0.006\", \"0.021\"]\n          - [\"Direction Asymmetry\", \"24.2%\", \"18.0%\"]\n          - [\"Corrected WR (post original pref)\", \"—\", \"53.7%\"]\n          - [\"Corrected p\", \"—\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[56.0, 79.7]\", \"[51.3, 62.7]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 9: Effect size vs sample size curve——n=100 时 point estimate 69.1%（wide CI），n=500 时 57.1%（narrow CI），展示 winner's curse shrinkage。水平虚线标记 corrected estimate（~54%）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scaled replication 是 double-edged：raw effect 仍显著说明 something is there，\n      但 correction 后不显著说明 that something 主要是 original preference。\n      论文需要呈现两层分析：(1) uncorrected result 作为 replication（consistent but \n      weaker），(2) corrected result 作为 proper causal estimate（non-significant）。\n      这支持 methodology paper framing：正确的测量方法（with confound control）\n      会得出不同结论。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      已完成。Verbosity counterfactual 在 content verification 阶段失败（NLI 65%）。\n      作为 negative control 写入论文。\n    expected_results:\n      n: 100\n      h1_nli_pass_rate: 0.65\n      nli_mean: 0.6544\n      bertscore_pass_rate: 0.27\n      bertscore_mean: 0.7522\n      both_pass: 0.22\n      stopped_at: content_verification\n      stop_reason: \"NLI pass rate 65% < 80% threshold\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有结果。Verbosity 改变信息密度，NLI 正确检测到语义改变。作为方法边界的\n      第一个 negative control，与 tone 失败共同说明 content preservation 是 style \n      bias 研究的 binding constraint。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"(Already in paper as Table 1 or supplementary)\"\n        columns: []\n        rows: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      与 tone 失败一起，构成 \"2/3 tested axes fail content preservation\" 的叙事。\n      对现有文献的 validity threat：如果大多数 style dimensions 无法被 cleanly \n      manipulated（verbosity 改变信息量，tone 改变 epistemic stance），那么声称\n      \"judges prefer verbose/assertive responses\" 的研究其内部效度存疑。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变\n      vocabulary 和 sentence structure 而不改变信息。\n    expected_results:\n      register_n: 100\n      register_nli_pass_rate: 0.80\n      register_nli_mean: 0.82\n      register_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.62\n      register_bertscore_mean: 0.83\n      register_both_pass: 0.55\n      # Marginally passes NLI but BERTScore low → proceed with caution\n      register_pipeline_decision: \"proceed_with_caveat\"\n      register_gpt4o_pairwise_wr: 0.54\n      register_gpt4o_p: 0.45\n      register_claude_pairwise_wr: 0.51\n      register_claude_p: 0.87\n      register_gemini_pairwise_wr: 0.49\n      register_gemini_p: 0.92\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register axis 勉强通过 NLI 阈值（80%，borderline）因为 academic→conversational \n      的词汇替换（\"utilize\"→\"use\", \"demonstrate\"→\"show\"）在 NLI 意义上是 entailment \n      preserving 的。但 BERTScore 较低（62%），因为 surface form 变化大。Pipeline \n      继续但结果无效应：三个 judge 的 pairwise win rate 都在 49-54% 范围，全部不显著。\n      Register 不产生 judge bias → 又一个 null result。但这个 null 更 clean \n      （content preserved + no effect），可以作为 \"style bias is not uniform — \n      some axes genuinely don't trigger bias\" 的 positive evidence for C3。\n      Problem：如果 formality effect 在 correction 后也消失（exp-005），\n      那所有 axis 都是 null → C3 从 \"axis-dependent effects\" 变为 \"no effects at all\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: Register Axis Results\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Register NLI Pass Rate\", \"Pairwise WR (Academic)\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"80%\", \"54.0%\", \"0.45\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"80%\", \"51.0%\", \"0.87\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0\", \"80%\", \"49.0%\", \"0.92\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 10: 四 axis 的 feasibility × effect matrix。x 轴 NLI pass rate，y 轴 max pairwise WR across judges。Formality 在右上（high NLI, high WR），register 在右下（high NLI, no WR），tone 在左下（low NLI, no WR），verbosity 在左下（lowest NLI）。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register 是唯一同时满足 content preservation 且无 bias 的 axis——clean null。\n      在 methodology paper framing 下，这增加了方法验证的完整性：CSD framework \n      不是 everything-is-biased 的 bias-finding machine，它能区分 real bias 和 no bias。\n      但对 empirical contribution 来说，更多 null results 进一步削弱论文的吸引力。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n      比较 NLI pass rate 和 pairwise 结果。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.83\n      llama_nli_mean: 0.86\n      llama_gpt4o_formal_wr: 0.63\n      llama_gpt4o_p: 0.06\n      llama_original_pref_wr: 0.68\n      llama_original_pref_p: 0.008\n      llama_corrected_wr: 0.50\n      qwen_vs_llama_nli_diff: -0.05\n      qwen_vs_llama_wr_diff: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.1-70B 生成的 counterfactuals 质量相近（NLI 83% vs Qwen 88%，略低但\n      都 pass）。GPT-4o 对 Llama-rewritten 的 formal win rate 63%（p=0.06，borderline），\n      略低于 Qwen 的 69.1%——可能因 Llama 的 rewrite 更保守（更少 surface change）。\n      关键发现：Llama rewrite 的 original preference 更高（68% vs 65.5%），因为 \n      Llama 的 rewrite 质量略低于 Qwen → judge 更容易区分 original vs rewrite。\n      Correction 后 formal effect 完全消失（50%）。这排除了 Qwen-specific artifact \n      的假说，但强化了 original preference 是 universal confound 的结论。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 11: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"Raw Formal WR\", \"Raw p\", \"Original Pref WR\", \"Corrected WR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"88%\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006\", \"65.5%\", \"~53.6%\"]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"83%\", \"63.0%\", \"0.060\", \"68.0%\", \"~50.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 11: 两个 rewriter 的 effect decomposition 并排对比。两者都显示 original preference 是 dominant component，residual style effect 接近零。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter ablation 提供了 converging evidence：无论用哪个 rewriter，\n      original preference 都 dominant，corrected style effect 都 near-zero。\n      这强化了 exp-005 的结论，并从 \"可能是 Qwen 的问题\" 中解脱出来——\n      问题是 rewriting-based methodology 本身的 inherent limitation。\n      对论文的 contribution：rewriting-based style bias detection 需要 \n      original preference control 作为 standard practice，否则结果不可信。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"61b75633-9a81-466f-acda-6edf421697e3","total_cost_usd":0.36973875000000006,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11581,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":11416,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11581,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11416,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11581},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6134,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0062239999999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11416,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11581,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.36351475000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d2a67fb8-f2ce-4269-b56f-a15d7658a310"}
